## Using sftp from pc to z/OS

### Using sftp on PC

Using Port 2022 and then your userid followed by the cbt IP address. In
this example I'm using a hostname I've defined in my PC's hostname file
so I don't have to remember the IP address.

Then using the `ls /+` syntax define the DCB and dsorg.

Next change the remote location to my TSO hlq and `put` the file.

*Note* by default `sftp` does a binary transfer, use `ls /+ mode=text`
to do a text transfer.


```
d:\temp>sftp -P 2022 lbdyck1@cbt
lbdyck1@cbt's password:
Connected to cbt.
sftp> ls /+ recfm=-fb,lrecl=80,blksize=0,dsorg=ps
/+/blksize=0     /+/dsorg=ps      /+/error.log     /+/gdgnt
/+/ispfenq       /+/ispfstats     /+/loglevel=I
/+/lrecl=80      /+/mode=binary
sftp> cd //lbdyck1
sftp> put VUELOAD.xmi*
Uploading VUELOAD.xmit to //LBDYCK1/VUELOAD.xmit
VUELOAD.xmit                               00%  709KB   1.1MB/s   00:00
sftp> quit
```

